<p>Ukraine’s High Anti-Corruption Court on Thursday ordered Andriy Yermak, President Volodymyr Zelenskyy’s former chief of staff, held in pretrial detention for two months and set bail at 140 million hryvnias, or about $3 million to $3.2 million. Yermak, once one of the most powerful figures in Zelenskyy’s administration, denies the allegations and said after the ruling that his lawyers would appeal. The National Anti-Corruption Bureau of Ukraine and the Specialized Anti-Corruption Prosecutor’s Office named Yermak a suspect earlier this week in a case involving an organized group accused of laundering about 460 million hryvnias, or roughly $10 million, through a luxury real estate project near Kyiv. The allegations are part of the wider Midas investigation, a corruption case that reports have linked to Ukraine’s energy sector and to figures including businessman Timur Mindich and former Deputy Prime Minister Oleksiy Chernyshov. Yermak resigned in November 2025 after investigators searched his home as the inquiry widened. Euronews reported that Zelenskyy had not commented on the case against his former aide.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/wnXWwhoCh3G8G6yxsiIbp0a6Y4DsKyzNU8CyT3FsYy4By6yWFL4uWP72xJ8C7oLjp90i_WNnNLphQVOQa5JsFwYlUUCJFWZDRI9ctjbm3CV3zHbwohYC6R9b2TBql6SL4uAa9wr9Cx9VmlnhG9l6J7lChJHvWRAyRR9mm2AYN8Y9qbaMus1s6vM0HOAv8ncVgficrg95zTQWR_6KPPjZhizGtE48SKrxyrgxGKI2CM7NH0oCSppv7EZ7DQgdWNzInMS8Xqc' alt='Andriy Yermak appears in court in Kyiv on May 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Hearing timing: The ruling came on the third day of hearings in Kyiv.</li><li>Bail dispute: Prosecutors sought 180 million hryvnias in bail, but the court imposed a lower amount after the defense argued that bail should reflect Yermak’s declared income.</li><li>Prosecution argument: Prosecutors argued that electronic monitoring alone would not prevent Yermak from interfering with the investigation.</li><li>Wartime role: Before he resigned, Yermak helped shape Ukraine’s wartime diplomacy and regularly appeared in high-level meetings with foreign leaders in Washington and Brussels.</li></ul><blockquote>I don’t have such funds. Now my lawyer will work with my friends for help - Andriy Yermak</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Andriy Yermak: Yermak said he would remain in Ukraine as the case proceeds. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/zelenskyy-former-top-aide-yermak-detained-corruption-charges-3-million-dollar-bail/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian anti-corruption prosecutors: Prosecutors linked the proposed bail level to the estimated cost of one house in the Kyiv-area luxury project that investigators say formed part of the laundering scheme. (<a href='https://istories.media/news/2026/05/14/eks-glavu-ofisa-zelenskogo-arestovali-pod-zalog-v-4-milliona-dollarov/'>Important Stories</a>)</li><li>National Anti-Corruption Bureau of Ukraine: NABU said Zelenskyy was not a subject of investigation in the case. (<a href='https://ct24.ceskatelevize.cz/clanek/svet/ukrajinsky-soud-poslal-exsefa-prezidentske-kancelare-jermaka-do-vazby-373415'>Czech Television</a>)</li><li>Ukrainian presidential office: The presidential office said it does not deal with esotericism, numerology or feng shui. (<a href='https://kurier.at/politik/ausland/ukraine-jermak-haft/403159775'>Kurier</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/zelenskyy-former-top-aide-yermak-detained-corruption-charges-3-million-dollar-bail/'>Zelenskyy’s former top aide locked up on corruption charges, with bail set at $3M</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3353586/ukraine-arrests-zelenskys-ex-top-aide-corruption-probe-widens'>Ukraine arrests Zelensky’s ex-top aide as corruption probe widens</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639973-yermak-corruption-hearings-bail/'>Ex-Zelensky aide ordered to pay $3.2 million bail as corruption case opens</a> - rt.com</li><li><a h